title ALES112 — Lotus's duplicate, repeat a span in place (the growth-twin of crop)
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; after ALES111 sent, take the next agent-doable Lotus lap, self-approve, prove GREEN, send as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think ALES111's crop keeps a span and drops the rest — the clip SHRINKS to the selection. Its clean growth-twin is duplicate: repeat one span in place, the clip GROWING by exactly the span. Circle a bar, press Duplicate, and a second copy lands immediately after the first — the doubled drum loop, the repeated chorus, the stutter edit. Naming it beside crop completes the shrink/grow pair on a selection: keep only it, or repeat it. Universal DAW gesture, Lindy-durable, and absent from the suite (checked: no duplicate/repeat).
think Shape: duplicate(clip, start, count) opens count silent seats at the span's end (end = start+count) through ALES109's insert_silence — a bounded grow that refuses ClipFull past the fixed buffer — then copies the original span FORWARD into that gap. Source [start, end) and dest [end, end+count) are adjacent and DISJOINT, dest ahead of source, so the forward copy is exact with NO temporary buffer (the aliasing trap avoided by inserting zeros first, then filling). Reuses timeline.EditError whole — BadRange when start > len or count > len - start, checked without underflow.
think Four laws: the DUPLICATE law (the clip becomes original[0..end] ++ original[start..end] ++ original[end..len), the length grown by count, proven at mid/head/tail); the INVERSE law — the crux tying it to ALES2: duplicate(start,count) then cut(end,count) returns the original byte for byte, the inserted copy removed exactly; the COPY / PEAK law (duplicate copies existing samples and invents none, so the peak re-measured through ALES13 is unchanged — the loud sample inside the span appears twice at the same magnitude, outside it untouched); the DEGENERATE / REFUSAL law (count 0 the identity, a span past the samples BadRange, and a grow past the fixed buffer ClipFull — proven by filling the clip to max_clip then a duplicate refusing, the length unchanged).
obs Witness GREEN on the first pass — all four laws, both BadRange branches, and the ClipFull branch (filled to max_clip = 4*1024 = 4096, then a one-sample duplicate refused, the length verified unchanged). Standing on insert_silence (ALES109) rather than open-coding the gap keeps the grow bounded and ClipFull-guarded in ONE place — duplicate is literally "open a gap after the span, then fill it with a copy," so it can never drift from the proven insert. The inverse law is the crux of the teaching: proving cut(end,count) undoes duplicate exactly makes remove and repeat read as a matched pair. TAME style bans clean (ratchet zero-assert count unchanged); >=2 positive-invariant asserts per fn; width-check clean; no new arithmetic invented; timeline.EditError reused whole. No custody gate touched — pure-Rye local i16 buffer, siloed to lotus/.
